    {
      "id": "65aefe7ac240614c952208cad9764451c38e70dfd9cbd3668759427db7edd01a",
      "text": "released a new open standard",
      "hash": "d6b25461f2b7f80515118bc42706c4062a7bf3fd01ba64f1066dc2c2bb0513d1"
    },
    {
      "id": "c57ba7085f071f5b91b979ca5260f3d6c64bc6e88460ea5961a7dfa810ca815f",
      "text": "for connecting \"AI assistants to the systems where data lives\".",
      "hash": "9cb461d1173aeaaec7dba031483049e4724606b1d6159be26dd3e8d1856f4c30"
    },
    {
      "id": "b08e24b75db935b528c7769ad2aaed810429f7387b33b29e4613d370a6d69ee6",
      "text": "It's a JSON-RPC-based protocol that lets an LLM (in this case, Claude) communicate with a long-running server. Claude can request what different tools are available to use, and then call them.",
      "hash": "b12d04f59371b30f976f95a832b501be032c1d334f5e2cf26600dbcbffa4abf0"
    },
    {
      "id": "35ce77ddc67a5e90c47de14d12a1e2ac2082205f411d75952d9649c70d5f66c1",
      "text": "There's a TypeScript and Python SDK, meaning you can easily create your own MCP servers to connect to your own data sources, or perform custom actions.",
      "hash": "3c6156aae9f96524478ea04c658ace5a4592b1658ad1964f089779b4c92a3c6f"
    },
